\ ==== text-width ====

\ text-width ( str -- n ): the width in pixels that print-at gives str in
\ Tigr's proportional built-in font, its widest line when it has several;
\ {name} colour directives and terminal escapes take no width. No window is
\ opened.

\ === single lines ===
"W" text-width . "i" text-width . "" text-width . cr       \ 8 3 0
"M.P.H." text-width . "AB" text-width . cr                 \ 31 14
clear

\ === directives take no width ===
"{red}AB" text-width . "A{dodgerblue}B{plain}" text-width . cr \ 14 14
clear

\ === the widest line ===
"AB{nl}ABCD" format text-width . "ABCD{nl}AB" format text-width . "{nl}" format text-width . cr \ 28 28 0
clear

\ errors
42 text-width                                              \ (not a string)
